{aligned}5 & k \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}|$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186441147 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1485a2c5-d3d5-5ae7-bfda-a8f34f74aef0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441147 #edb/ref 1074 "The determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & k \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $x$ is given by $x=\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x} & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & k \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D} \\\\ 2 & =\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}5 & k \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}4 & k \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|} \\\\ 2|\\begin{aligned}4 & k \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & k \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only\"." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186464078 #edb/ref 1080 "false" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186464078 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186464078 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8504eb0f-93c6-5d20-8195-88dbad00b315" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186464079 #edb/ref 1080 "true" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186464079 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186464079 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c70ffc2d-dbef-5e28-8e5a-6e4a97b209b2" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186464080 #edb/ref 1080 "false" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186464080 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186464080 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "855711cd-7b19-555c-ab6e-e3cbe95bee72" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186464081 #edb/ref 1080 "true" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186464081 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186464081 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8f8516b4-64ce-53f5-938e-8dfecd51f520" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186464082 #edb/ref 1080 "false" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186464082 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 1